<div class="gb-page">

  <header class="gb-header">
    <div class="gb-eyebrow">The Power Law &middot; in another unit</div>
    <h1>Bitcoin, priced in <em>gold</em></h1>
    <p class="gb-subtitle">The Power Law is usually drawn in dollars. Measure bitcoin in ounces of gold instead and the same kind of trend appears, a little looser. This page shows where bitcoin sits against it today, and why that differs from the dollar picture.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="gb-attribution">
    <div class="gb-attribution-label">Lineage &amp; attribution</div>
    <p>Pricing bitcoin&rsquo;s power law in gold is not new. <strong>Matthew Mezinskis</strong> (<a href="https://www.porkopolis.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Porkopolis Economics</a>) has charted bitcoin against gold alongside his dollar work, <strong>Stephen Perrenod</strong> published a fit in ounces in 2024 (<a href="https://stephenperrenod.substack.com/p/bitcoin-power-law-vs-gold-mid-2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exponent 5.47 on quarterly prices</a>), and <a href="https://b1m.io/gold" target="_blank" rel="noopener">b1m.io</a> tracks one live. The fit, the range and the comparisons below are this site&rsquo;s own, computed from the World Bank&rsquo;s monthly gold series and the site&rsquo;s bitcoin price record.</p>
  </div>

