  <!-- §4 WHY THEY PARTED -->
  <section class="gb-section">
    <h2>Why the lines parted</h2>
    <p>Mostly, gold moved. Its monthly average went from <span id="gbGold2024">&mdash;</span> an ounce in January 2024 to <span id="gbGoldPeak">&mdash;</span> in <span id="gbGoldPeakWhen">&mdash;</span>, <span id="gbGoldRunX">&mdash;</span> in a little over two years, and stood at <span id="gbGoldLast">&mdash;</span> in <span id="gbGoldLastWhen">&mdash;</span>. Over the same stretch bitcoin made a new high in October 2025, when it bought about <span id="gbOzAtHigh">&mdash;</span> ounces, and then fell. Today it buys about <span id="gbOzToday2">&mdash;</span>, <span id="gbOzFall">&mdash;</span> fewer ounces than at that high, against a <span id="gbUsdFall">&mdash;</span> fall in dollars.</p>
    <p id="gbPartedRead"></p>
  </section>

  <!-- §5 HOW STURDY -->
  <section class="gb-section">
    <h2>How sturdy is the gold trend?</h2>
    <p>A trend is only as good as its stability. Fit it from a later start and see whether it holds. Here are the four starting years, in both units, with today&rsquo;s reading against each; the highlighted row is the one the page is using.</p>
